Tom: Good afternoon.Muje tumhara contact meri colleague Anna se mila. Diana: Hello Tom, it's good to hear from you. Anna ne bola tha tumse baat hogi. How can I help you? Tom: Actually, Do cheeze hai. First of all, my wife and I are looking for a flat. At the same time humein apna purana flat bhi bechna hai. Diana: I understand. Thank you for contacting me, Mai aapki help kardungi. Are you looking for a flat to buy or to rent? Tom: This is one of the things we've been discussing with my wife. Ajkal ke trends kya hai? Aap kaunsa option suggest karengi? Diana: It depends on what you value more, Sunne mai obvious hoga, agar aap stability ko flexibility se zyada value dete hain , I would suggest you invest in buying a flat. Tom: Hume kuch bada chaiye bigger than what we own now, but Humare paas budget nahi rahega for something we may need in the future. Diana: Is case mein, I would suggest maybe Kuch chota khareedie for rent and renting at the same time a small flat to save or buying something slightly below the budget, Jisse aap future ke lie save karlo. Tom: Thank you! Ye acchi advice hai ! Tom: I will talk to my wife, but abhi ke lie , I think we could focus on buying something similar size. Diana: Apko kitne rooms chaiye? Tom: Two bedrooms at least, joined kitchen and living room ho to accha hai. Diana: Apki koi preferred neighbourhood hai? Tom: Anywhere near the tube station within zone 3 is acceptable. Diana: Thank you. Aapka current budget kya hai? Tom: Humlog about £400 000 ka soch rahe the. possible ho paaega? Diana: Haan shayad. Aapko aisa flat chalega jisme thoda renovation ki zaroorat ho? Tom: It depends on hum apna flat kitne mai bech rahe hain. Diana: aap kitna target kar rahe hain? Tom: At least £300 000, flat ki condition kaafi acchhi hai, neighbourhood achha hai aur 1 saal pehle hi renovate hua hai. Diana: Could you please send me some pictures? Mai apke saath appointment bhi set karti hu. Tom: Haan That would be perfect! Diana: Kya Monday ko 8bje chalega? Tom: Hm, Mujhe apni wife se ek baar consult karna hai, but so far Chalega.
